skill: "linkedin-company-pages"
sections[10]:
  - "\n"
  - "# linkedin-company-pages\n\nThe **company-page (LINKEDIN_PAGES) strategy** — treat the page as a **credibility hub + paid launchpad** and\nbuild the real organic engine, **employee advocacy.** The agent **strategizes + designs the advocacy program\n+ drafts page posts + drafts shareable content**; **WoopSocial publishes the page's own posts**; **employees\npost from their own profiles, and the first-hour engagement, paid, and native features are human/native.**\n\n"
  - "## The POV: a credibility hub + paid launchpad, not the reach engine\nLinkedIn **structurally rebalanced** the feed — **company pages get ~1–5% of feed allocation** (personal\nprofiles ~65%) and **page organic reach fell 60–66% since 2024.** So the page's real jobs are **credibility,\nthe official record, recruitment, and the paid launchpad** (LinkedIn Ads + **Thought Leader Ads** run\nexclusively from it) — **not** organic reach. **People connect with people, not logos:** the algorithm trusts\nindividuals over brands, so the organic growth engine is **employee advocacy** (employees have ~10× the\nconnections; ~3% who share drive ~30% of engagement; employee leads convert ~7×). WoopSocial publishes the\npage's **own** posts; the **advocacy runs through employees' personal profiles.**\n\n"
  - "## Read these first\n1. **brand-profile** — positioning/voice.\n2. **goals-and-kpis** — awareness vs hiring vs pipeline.\n\n"
  - "## The framework: HUMAN\n(Depth: `references/the-human-framework.md`.)\n- **H — Hub, not megaphone:** the page = credibility hub + paid launchpad (Ads/Thought Leader Ads,\n  announcements, recruitment, Follow button) — not the reach engine; set honest expectations.\n- **U — Unleash employee advocacy:** the primary organic lever (people not logos; ~10× connections, 3% →\n  30%, ~5× leads); a **frictionless program** (shareable content + suggested commentary employees\n  **personalize, not identical**, Notify Employees, a pilot, light gamification, leadership math); employees\n  post from their **own profiles** (→ `linkedin-growth`).\n- **M — Move in the first hour:** employees engaging within ~60 min is a strong reach signal; coordinate;\n  executive/CEO content ~4× the page.\n- **A — Anchor page-appropriate content:** carousel/document (top saves), short vertical video w/ captions,\n  custom images — **never text-only** (~0.42×); **links in comments, not body** (−60%); questions/frameworks\n  → 437% views + saves (Depth Score). (Post craft → `linkedin-post-writer`; visuals → `ideogram`/`nano-banana`.)\n- **N — Nurture cadence + measure:** consistent (weekly+) → ~5.6× followers; respond fast; track followers,\n  reach, engagement, **advocacy UTM conversions**; no bait/pods/forced-identical/bought followers.\n\n"
  - "## The reality (verify-quarterly)\nStructural rebalance (pages ~1–5% feed, reach −60–66%); personal 5–8× engagement (conservative Sprout ~4.7%\nvs ~1–2%); people-not-logos (3× trust, 92% buyers trust employees); the page's real jobs + the paid launchpad\n(Ads/Thought Leader Ads exclusive); content assignment (page vs personal vs both); employee advocacy = the\nlever (10× connections, 3%→30%, 2.75×/5×, 7× conversion, first-hour signal, CEO 4×, program design); page\ncontent (carousel/document, short video, custom image, no text-only 0.42×, links-in-comments −60%, questions\n437%, saves, Depth Score); cadence (weekly 5.6×, 150-follower threshold); native features (Notify Employees/\nShowcase/Events/Newsletters/Thought-Leader-Ads/BrandWorks): `references/company-pages-2026-reality.md`. The\nadvocacy program blueprint, page content-type table, content-assignment matrix + worked examples:\n`references/advocacy-and-content-plays.md`.\n\n"
  - "## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **The agent** strategizes the page, **designs the advocacy program**, **drafts page posts**, and **drafts\n  shareable advocacy content + commentary.**\n- **WoopSocial publishes** the **company page's OWN posts** (`LINKEDIN_PAGES`: text + media + optional `link`;\n  **no native document/carousel/poll field**) on a **schedule**.\n- **WoopSocial does NOT:** post from **employees' personal profiles** (the growth engine — **human**, →\n  `linkedin-growth`), do the **first-hour engagement** (human), run **Ads / Thought Leader Ads** (native\n  paid), build **native document/carousel** posts (native), or run **Notify Employees / Showcase / Events /\n  Newsletters / Page analytics** (native).\n- **No engagement-bait/pods/forced-identical/bought followers**; **links in comments, not body**; **organic\n  page reach is genuinely low** (page = credibility + paid launchpad); **never fabricate metrics.** (Scope,\n  distinctions + connections: `references/scope-and-connections.md`.)\n\n"
  - "## Distinct from its siblings (route correctly)\n**linkedin-company-pages (this)** = the COMPANY-PAGE strategy (credibility hub + paid launchpad + employee-\nadvocacy program) · **linkedin-growth** = the PERSONAL profile strategy (where reach is + where advocacy\nposting routes) · **linkedin-post-writer** = the single-post craft · **social-selling-and-dm** = DM/outreach ·\n**ugc-and-influencer**/**collabs-and-cross-promotion** = external creators (BrandWorks).\n\n"
  - "## Where this connects\nReads first: **brand-profile**, **goals-and-kpis**. Routes craft to: **linkedin-post-writer** (the page post),\n**ideogram**/**nano-banana** (carousel/video visuals), **linkedin-growth** (the employees'/founder's personal-\nprofile advocacy — the engine), **caption-writer** (lines). Pairs with: **social-selling-and-dm** (pipeline),\n**lead-magnets-and-funnels**/**email-and-newsletter** (the gated assets the page links to via comments),\n**campaign-and-launch-planning** (launches), **analytics-and-reporting** (page + advocacy UTM readout).\nPublishes via: **scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial** (the page's own posts) + **platform-specs-and-validation**.\nEmployee posting, the first-hour engagement, paid, and native features stay human/native.\n\n"
  - "## Definition of done\nThe page positioned as a credibility hub + paid launchpad (not the reach engine), with honest expectations\nabout ~1–5% organic reach; an employee-advocacy program designed as the primary organic lever (frictionless\nkit, personalized-not-identical commentary, Notify Employees, a pilot, first-hour coordination) with the\nemployees' personal-profile craft routed to linkedin-growth; page-appropriate content (carousel/document,\nshort video, custom images — never text-only; links in comments; questions/frameworks) routed to\nlinkedin-post-writer and the image tools; a weekly+ cadence and metrics defined (followers, reach, engagement,\nadvocacy UTM conversions); the page's own posts published via WoopSocial while employee posting, first-hour\nengagement, paid, and native features stay human/native; no bait/pods/forced-identical/bought followers,\nnothing fabricated; correctly distinguished from linkedin-growth and linkedin-post-writer.\n"
